Finding: both 30-second request layers delete correlation and reject locally without a cancellation/indeterminate/admission contract. A normal cold operation can continue and commit after HTTP 500. The governing mechanism predates and is blob-identical to the reviewed base; the Socratic ticket delta changes only the logical address shape, and the same failure reproduces through unchanged Brief launch.
Classification: Design Impact -> /solution_designer. Raising a timeout alone would preserve the ambiguous-commit defect and is not an adequate local fix.
